  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: Our best result so far is config_016 (multimodal, single-profile, PCA n2000, ResNet50, concat) at 0.527 acc, modestly above RNA-only (0.485) and far above image-only (0.208). The concat vs weighted difference is negligible (~0.3%), so fusion type is a minor factor. The major untested design axis is single-profile vs multiprofile, which could substantially change how both modalities contribute. This experiment (config_018) extends our best configuration to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation and concat fusion, keeping all other variables identical to config_016. It directly tests whether multiprofile representation (with simple average pooling) improves over single-profile, resolving a key uncertainty before committing budget to more complex aggregation strategies (transformer) or alternative encoders. If multiprofile helps, it opens the aggregation-strategy question for all future experiments; if it does not, we can confidently focus on single-profile variants and encoder improvements, saving limited budget."
}

